            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>This Week's Update: Platform Scrutiny Intensifies, Pressure Mounts on Multi-Account Teams</h2>
<p>This week, multiple overseas marketing teams reported a noticeable increase in Meta ad account reviews. Some accounts received "account restricted" notifications without warning, causing running campaigns to suddenly pause. One operations director revealed: "Our multiple accounts with daily spend exceeding $20,000 were simultaneously throttled, resulting in direct losses exceeding $150,000."</p>
<p>This is not an isolated incident. As platform risk control algorithms continue to evolve, "correlation risks" in multi-account management are being identified more precisely. The crude management model simply pursuing account quantity is no longer sustainable.</p>
<h2>Core Logic of Account Tiering Management</h2>
<p>Account tiering is not simply "dividing accounts" but rather graded management of advertising assets with the goals of risk isolation and resource optimization.</p>
<h3>Tier Dimensions Reference</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Tier</th>
<th>Account Type</th>
<th>Characteristics</th>
<th>Management Focus</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Tier 1</td>
<td>Core Main Accounts</td>
<td>Long-term stable, high spend, good conversions</td>
<td>Protect account health, limit high-frequency operations</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Tier 2</td>
<td>Testing Accounts</td>
<td>Newly created, low spend, exploring new creatives</td>
<td>Allow for trial and error, rapid iteration</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Tier 3</td>
<td>Backup Accounts</td>
<td>Under observation or with restricted history</td>
<td>Budget-limited, risk-isolated</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Practical Recommendations: Three-Tier Isolation Method</h3>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>IP and Device Isolation</strong>: Use independent devices for main accounts and testing accounts, avoiding cross-contamination of correlation factors like cookies and browser fingerprints. One utility app team's approach was equipping main accounts with cloud servers with fixed IPs, while testing accounts used local networks.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Diversified Payment Sources</strong>: Don't fund all accounts from the same credit card. Operations experience from Yiyu Media shows that spreading funding sources across 3-5 payment channels can effectively reduce the platform's judgment of account correlation.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>梯级 Budget Configuration</strong>: Main account daily budget should not exceed 150% of the account's historical average spend, while testing accounts can have exploration budgets of $200-500. Risk hedging is achieved through budget differences.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Creative and Copy Differentiation</strong>: Don't directly copy the same high-converting creatives across all accounts. It's recommended that main accounts use verified creatives while testing accounts bear the responsibility of new creative verification.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h2>Impact Assessment This Week</h2>
<p>For teams that have established tiering management mechanisms, the impact of this platform review tightening has been relatively controllable. The performance difference between these two types of teams is notable:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Teams with proper tiering</strong>: Main accounts were basically unaffected; testing accounts absorbed the main impact of this risk control, with overall spend fluctuation within 10%.</li>
<li><strong>Teams without tiering</strong>: After some accounts were throttled, overall budget cuts became necessary, with recovery period estimated at 1-2 weeks.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Editor's Recommendations</h2>
<p>Multi-account performance teams should view account tiering management as a routine risk control practice, not an emergency response after problems occur. Consider completing the following two checks this week:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Account Health Audit</strong>: Review all running accounts' spend history, review records, and violation situations, flag accounts requiring downgrading or isolation.</li>
<li><strong>Payment Path Audit</strong>: Check whether account funding sources are overly concentrated, and proactively plan payment channel diversification.</li>
</ul>
<p>The essence of multi-account management is risk management. Clear tiering maintains strategic composure during platform risk control fluctuations.</p>
